 "reference": "Cross-language proof for the machine-learning surface. Every assertion uses exact equality and is replayed through C++, R, Python, and the real C# library. The seeded cases cover k-means++ initialization, RandomForest's separate bootstrap and feature streams, and k-NN bootstrap intervals. Numerics v2.2.0 replaced the parallel mean with a sequential reduction, so both mean columns are now pinned. Flat index 4 of the k-NN case remains omitted because fused multiply-add contraction in the shared C++ distance calculation differs from .NET by 2 ULP on that lower bound; the packages still agree with each other exactly.",
